[36m(TaskRunner pid=391279)[0m - \(3^b \equiv 1 \pmod{10}\) requires \(b \equiv 0 \pmod{4}\) or \(b \equiv 2 \pmod{4}\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=391279)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=391279)[0m However, since 9! includes 5 and 7 as prime factors, we need to ensure that the divisor does not introduce factors that would affect the units digit. The only valid divisors that satisfy the condition are 1 and 81, as they are 1 modulo 10 and are divisors of \(9!\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=391279)[0m 
